  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Without using your calculator, find the angles $\\theta$, between $0^\\circ$ and $360^\\circ$ inclusive, for which:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$225^\\circ,315^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Sine is negative in quadrants III and IV. Since $\\sin45^\\circ=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}$, the related angle is $45^\\circ$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ+45^\\circ\\text{ or }360^\\circ-45^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=225^\\circ\\text{ or }315^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta=-\\frac1{\\sqrt3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$150^\\circ,330^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Tangent is negative in quadrants II and IV. Since $\\tan30^\\circ=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}$, the related angle is $30^\\circ$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-30^\\circ\\text{ or }360^\\circ-30^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=150^\\circ\\text{ or }330^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$150^\\circ,210^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Cosine is negative in quadrants II and III. Since $\\cos30^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$, the related angle is $30^\\circ$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-30^\\circ\\text{ or }180^\\circ+30^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=150^\\circ\\text{ or }210^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$90^\\circ$",
          "worked": "On the unit circle, sine is the $y$-coordinate. The only point with $y=1$ is $(0,1)$, so $\\theta=90^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$90^\\circ,270^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Cosine is the $x$-coordinate on the unit circle. The points with $x=0$ are $(0,1)$ and $(0,-1)$, so $\\theta=90^\\circ$ or $270^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q2-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0^\\circ,180^\\circ,360^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Since $\\tan\\theta=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$, tangent is zero when $\\sin\\theta=0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$. In the inclusive interval, $\\theta=0^\\circ,180^\\circ$ or $360^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
  },
